{"step_index":66,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:30:15Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T18:30:15+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T18:30:16+02:00\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n<truncated 1 lines>\n                        continue\r\n\r\n                    dev_map = devices.nic_bridge(bridge_name, dev_name=\"eth0\")\r\n                    extra_config = {\r\n                        \"user.blueagent.team_k\": str(team_k),\r\n                        \"user.blueagent.spec_name\": c.name,\r\n                    }\r\n\r\n                    spec_copy = c.model_copy(update={\"name\": full_inst_name})\r\n                    logger.info(\"Creating container '%s' on bridge '%s'\", full_inst_name, bridge_name)\r\n                    t_create = time.perf_counter()\r\n                    await self.engine.create_instance(spec_copy, devices=dev_map, extra_config=extra_config)\r\n                    create_sec = time.perf_counter() - t_create\r\n                    created_instances.append(full_inst_name)\r\n\r\n                    # Inject network configurations\r\n                    t_push = time.perf_counter()\r\n                    networkd_conf = render_networkd_conf(ip=ip_addr, gateway=gateway_ip)\r\n                    await self.engine.push_file(\r\n                        full_inst_name,\r\n                        \"/etc/systemd/network/10-eth0.network\",\r\n                        networkd_conf,\r\n                        mode=\"0644\",\r\n                    )\r\n\r\n                    interfaces_conf = render_interfaces_conf(ip=ip_addr, gateway=gateway_ip)\r\n                    await self.engine.push_file(\r\n                        full_inst_name,\r\n                        \"/etc/network/interfaces\",\r\n                        interfaces_conf,\r\n                        mode=\"0644\",\r\n                    )\r\n\r\n                    await self.engine.push_file(\r\n                        full_inst_name,\r\n                        \"/etc/hostname\",\r\n                        f\"{c.name}\\n\",\r\n                        mode=\"0644\",\r\n                    )\r\n                    push_sec = time.perf_counter() - t_push\r\n\r\n                    # Start instance\r\n                    logger.info(\"Starting container '%s'\", full_inst_name)\r\n                    t_start = time.perf_counter()\r\n                    await self.engine.start_instance(full_inst_name)\r\n                    start_sec = time.perf_counter() - t_start\r\n\r\n                    t_net = time.perf_counter()\r\n                    try:\r\n                        await self.engine.exec_command(full_inst_name, ip.addr_replace(f\"{ip_addr}/24\", \"eth0\"))\r\n                        await self.engine.exec_command(full_inst_name, ip.link_up(\"eth0\"))\r\n                        await self.engine.exec_command(full_inst_name, ip.route_replace_default(gateway_ip, \"eth0\"))\r\n                    except Exception as net_err:\r\n                        logger.warning(\"Could not apply immediate runtime IP to %s: %s\", full_inst_name, net_err)\r\n                    runtime_net_sec = time.perf_counter() - t_net\r\n\r\n                    t_db = time.perf_counter()\r\n                    await self.db.record_container(\r\n                        instance_name=full_inst_name,\r\n                        team_k=team_k,\r\n                        spec_name=c.name,\r\n                        ip_address=ip_addr,\r\n                        image_alias=c.image,\r\n                    )\r\n                    db_record_sec = time.perf_counter() - t_db\r\n\r\n                    container_timings.append({\r\n                        \"container\": c.name,\r\n                        \"create_sec\": round(create_sec, 4),\r\n                        \"push_sec\": round(push_sec, 4),\r\n                        \"start_sec\": round(start_sec, 4),\r\n                        \"runtime_net_sec\": round(runtime_net_sec, 4),\r\n                        \"db_record_sec\": round(db_record_sec, 4),\r\n                        \"total_container_sec\": round(time.perf_counter() - c_t0, 4),\r\n                    })\r\n\r\n                team_containers = await self.db.list_team_containers(team_k)\r\n                now_dt = datetime.now(timezone.utc)\r\n                deploy_total_sec = time.perf_counter() - t_deploy_start\r\n\r\n                step_timings = {\r\n                    \"validation_sec\": round(validation_sec, 4),\r\n                    \"total_create_sec\": round(sum(ct[\"create_sec\"] for ct in container_timings), 4),\r\n                    \"total_push_sec\": round(sum(ct[\"push_sec\"] for ct in container_timings), 4),\r\n                    \"total_start_sec\": round(sum(ct[\"start_sec\"] for ct in container_timings), 4),\r\n                    \"total_runtime_net_sec\": round(sum(ct[\"runtime_net_sec\"] for ct in container_timings), 4),\r\n                    \"total_db_record_sec\": round(sum(ct[\"db_record_sec\"] for ct in container_timings), 4),\r\n                    \"total_deploy_sec\": round(deploy_total_sec, 4),\r\n                    \"container_details\": container_timings,\r\n                }\r\n\r\n                return DeployResponse(\r\n                    team_k=team_k,\r\n                    challenge_id=config.challenge_id,\r\n                    status=\"running\",\r\n                    config_json=config.model_dump_json(),\r\n                    deployed_at=now_dt,\r\n                    updated_at=now_dt,\r\n                    containers=team_containers,\r\n                    instances=team_containers,\r\n                    step_timings=step_timings,\r\n                )\r\n\r\n            except Exception as deploy_err:\r\n                logger.exception(\r\n                    \"Challenge '%s' deployment failed on team %d, performing atomic rollback: %s\",\r\n                    config.challenge_id,\r\n                    team_k,\r\n                    deploy_err,\r\n                )\r\n                rollback_errors = []\r\n                for name in reversed(created_instances):\r\n                    try:\r\n                        logger.info(\"Rolling back instance '%s'\", name)\r\n                        await self.engine.delete_instance(name, force=True)\r\n                        await self.db.delete_container(name)\r\n                    except Exception as rb_exc:\r\n                        rollback_errors.append(f\"{name}: {rb_exc}\")\r\n\r\n                if not rollback_errors:\r\n                    raise DeploymentRollbackError(\r\n                        f\"Challenge deployment failed and was rolled back: {deploy_err}\"\r\n                    ) from deploy_err\r\n                else:\r\n                    raise DeploymentFailedError(\r\n                        f\"Challenge deployment failed and rollback encountered errors: {deploy_err}\"\r\n                    ) from deploy_err\r\n\r\n    async def teardown_challenge(\r\n        self,\r\n        team_k: int,\r\n        challenge_id: Optional[str] = \"ch\",\r\n        container_names: Optional[List[str]] = None,\r\n    ) -> None:\r\n        \"\"\"Tears down containers for team k within the team lock.\"\"\"\r\n        async with self.locks.lock_team(team_k):\r\n            team = await self.db.get_team_by_k(team_k)\r\n            if not team:\r\n                raise TeamNotFoundError(f\"Team {team_k} does not exist\")\r\n            await teardown_challenge(\r\n                challenge_id=challenge_id or \"ch\",\r\n                team_k=team_k,\r\n                db=self.db,\r\n                engine=self.engine,\r\n                container_names=container_names,\r\n            )\r\n\r\n    async def get_active_containers(self, team_k: int) -> List[RunningContainerRecord]:\r\n        \"\"\"Lists active containers for a team.\"\"\"\r\n        team = await self.db.get_team_by_k(team_k)\r\n        if not team:\r\n            raise TeamNotFoundError(f\"Team {team_k} does not exist\")\r\n        return await self.db.list_team_containers(team_k)\r\n\r\n    async def verify_challenge(self, team_k: int, config: ChallengeConfig) -> VerifyResultResp:\r\n        \"\"\"Executes verification against dark OVN sandbox clones with readiness checks.\"\"\"\r\n        try:\r\n            async with self.locks.acquire(\"verify\", str(team_k), timeout=0.01):\r\n                async with self.locks.lock_team(team_k, timeout=10.0):\r\n                    team = await self.db.get_team_by_k(team_k)\r\n                    if not team:\r\n                        raise TeamNotFoundError(f\"Team {team_k} does not exist\")\r\n\r\n                    session_id = str(team_k)\r\n                    verifier = OVNVerifier(self.engine, config, session_id, team_k=team_k)\r\n                    await verifier.__aenter__()\r\n\n"}
{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T16:30:16Z","input_tokens":2264,"cache_read_tokens":46024,"output_tokens":3114,"content":"Because [`ChallengeService.deploy_challenge`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/services/challenges.py#L106-L246) and [`OVNVerifier`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/verifier/ovn.py#L28-L296) already instrument sub-millisecond `time.perf_counter()` timers and return a `step_timings` breakdown in every API response, we can measure not just *total* latency, but **where every millisecond is spent**.\n\nBased on the code in [`challenges.py`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/services/challenges.py) and [`ovn.py`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/verifier/ovn.py) and the host hardware on `192.168.0.199` (**AMD Ryzen 7 7700X 8-Core, 15 GiB RAM, 1.88 GiB `blueagent-zfs` pool**), here are the **5 stress tests** I recommend and **why each one is critical**.\n\n---\n\n### What Happens Under the Hood (Why Timings Degrade)\n\nBefore testing, look at the exact operations BlueAgent performs per request:\n\n1. **Container Creation (`POST /teams/{team_k}/machines`):**\n   For *each* container sequentially in a `for` loop ([`challenges.py`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/services/challenges.py#L121-L214)):\n   - `create_sec`: ZFS CoW clone from base image via Incus UDS.\n   - `push_sec`: **3 sequential file pushes** (`10-eth0.network`, `/etc/network/interfaces`, `/etc/hostname`).\n   - `start_sec`: LXC container boot.\n   - `runtime_net_sec`: **3 sequential `incus exec` calls** (`ip addr replace`, `ip link up`, `ip route replace`).\n2. **Verification (`POST /teams/{team_k}/verificator`):**\n   Inside [`OVNVerifier`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/verifier/ovn.py#L46-L185):\n   - `ovn_network_create_sec`: Allocates OVN logical switch `verify-{team_k}` in `ovn-northd`.\n   - `total_clone_time_sec`: ZFS CoW snapshot copy of each live container (`c-{k}-{name}` $\\to$ `verify-{k}-{name}`).\n   - `total_connect_time_sec` + `total_start_time_sec` + `total_runtime_net_sec`: Rebinds `eth0` to OVN, boots clones, runs 3 `ip` commands per clone.\n   - `verifier_runner_sec`: Optional ephemeral black-box container creation & boot.\n   - `readiness_sec` + `verify_commands_sec`: Runs health probes and exploit/patch checks.\n   - `cleanup`: Force-stops & deletes clones + deletes OVN switch.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Stress Tests & Why\n\n#### Test 1: Single-Team Baseline & Micro-Phase Profiling ($M=1\\text{ team}, N=1\\text{ container}$)\n* **What to do:** Run 10 back-to-back cycles of `deploy` $\\to$ `verify (in-container)` $\\to$ `verify (with ephemeral verifier runner)` $\\to$ `teardown` for a single team with zero contention.\n* **Why:**\n  * Establishes the **best-case latency floor** (p50, p95, stddev) for every internal phase in `step_timings`.\n  * Quantifies the **overhead of spawning a black-box `verifier` runner** (`verifier_runner_sec`) vs. agentless in-container execution (`target: \"container\"`).\n  * Reveals whether the 3 sequential `push_file` + 3 sequential `exec_command` calls dominate container startup more than ZFS cloning itself.\n\n#### Test 2: Multi-Container Challenge Scaling ($M=1\\text{ team}, N \\in \\{1, 2, 4, 8\\}\\text{ containers per challenge}$)\n* **What to do:** Deploy and verify a single team whose challenge topology grows from 1 container (e.g., Web) to 2 (Web + DB), 4, and 8 containers.\n* **Why:**\n  * Both [`deploy_challenge`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/services/challenges.py#L121) and [`OVNVerifier.__aenter__`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/verifier/ovn.py#L64) iterate over `config.containers` **sequentially** (`for c in self.config.containers:`).\n  * This test measures the linear slope ($\\Delta t / \\text{container}$) for both creation and verification. If $N=4$ takes $4\\times$ longer than $N=1$, it proves that parallelizing per-container provisioning with `asyncio.gather` would yield an immediate speedup.\n\n#### Test 3: Cross-Team Concurrency Burst ($M \\in \\{1, 5, 10, 20, 30\\}\\text{ teams in parallel}$)\n* **What to do:** Fire $M$ simultaneous `POST /teams/{team_k}/machines` requests across $M$ distinct teams, followed by $M$ simultaneous `POST /teams/{team_k}/verificator` requests (`asyncio.gather` across teams $1..M$).\n* **Why:**\n  * This simulates a **CTF competition start** (all teams deploying at once) and a **submission rush** (multiple teams clicking \"Verify Patch\" simultaneously).\n  * Because per-team locks ([`locks.py`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/locks.py)) only block *within* the same `team_k`, cross-team requests run in parallel and hit three shared bottlenecks:\n    1. **Incus Unix Domain Socket (`/var/lib/incus/unix.socket`)** & Go daemon worker pool.\n    2. **ZFS pool I/O serialization** (`blueagent-zfs` on loopback disk).\n    3. **OVN Northbound DB (`ovn-northd`)** creating/deleting $M$ logical switches simultaneously.\n  * Shows the exact **knee of the curve** where p95 deploy/verify time spikes from seconds to timeouts.\n\n#### Test 4: Dirty Container Write Amplification (CoW vs. Mutated State)\n* **What to do:** Compare verification time on a pristine container vs. a container where the team wrote $50\\text{ MB} - 200\\text{ MB}$ of modified files/logs in `/var/log` or `/tmp`.\n* **Why:**\n  * BlueAgent relies on ZFS Copy-on-Write (`instance_only=True`) claiming ~100 ms cloning.\n  * Furthermore, `blueagent-zfs` on this machine has **only 1.87 GiB free**. This test verifies whether dirty filesystem state slows down `clone_sec` or `clones_teardown_sec`, and how many concurrent teams with mutated containers can exist before exhausting the 1.88 GiB ZFS pool.\n\n#### Test 5: Sustained Verification Soak & Same-Team Stampede\n* **What to do:**\n  1. **Stampede:** Send 20 concurrent `verificator` requests to the *same* `team_k` to measure the rejection latency of the 19 `HTTP 409 Conflict` responses (ensuring the `0.01s` lock timeout in [`challenges.py`](file:///home/debian/bluectfd/blueagent/src/blueagent/services/challenges.py#L266) doesn't block the event loop).\n  2. **Soak:** Run 50 consecutive verifications across 5 teams and check `incus list`, `incus network list`, and `zpool list` afterward.\n* **Why:**\n  * Validates that `cleanup` (`clones_teardown_sec` + `ovn_network_delete_sec`) leaves **zero leaked ZFS snapshots, orphaned `verify-*` containers, or dangling OVN switches**, and that verify times don't progressively degrade over a long CTF.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table of Metrics We Will Collect\n\n| Metric | Source in BlueAgent | What It Tells Us |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Deploy Total & Breakdown** | `DeployResponse.step_timings` (`create_sec`, `push_sec`, `start_sec`, `runtime_net_sec`) | Exact container creation speed & bottleneck phase |\n| **Verify Setup Time** | `VerifyResultResp.details.step_timings.setup` (`ovn_network_create_sec`, `total_clone_time_sec`, `total_start_time_sec`) | Cost of spinning up the isolated OVN dark sandbox |\n| **Verify Probe Time** | `readiness_sec` + `verify_commands_sec` | Overhead of `incus exec` polling and exploit execution |\n| **Verify Teardown Time** | `cleanup.total_cleanup_sec` | Hidden time paid before HTTP response returns to CTFd |\n| **Host CPU / RAM / ZFS** | `/proc/stat`, `/proc/meminfo`, `zpool list` | Hardware saturation point during parallel bursts |\n\nWould you like me to set up the Python environment on `192.168.0.199` and build/run a benchmark script that executes these stress tests and generates a full timing report?","thinking":"Initial analysis reveals that challenge deployment and verification processes include recording mechanisms. This suggests existing infrastructure for tracking relevant data related to these actions. This information can be leveraged for debugging or auditing.\n\n\nDeployment and verification timings are now available at a granular level. Container creation metrics include instance creation, file pushes, startup, network configuration, and database record duration. Verification data captures OVN network creation, ZFS clone time, interface rebinding, clone startup, and network configuration execution. This detailed information will be crucial for performance analysis and optimization.\n\n\nObserved that container provisioning and verification steps are sequential within a challenge, limiting parallelism. Bottleneck identified in sequential calls for file pushes and command execution per container, along with overall instance creation. Potential constraint on ZFS pool size could impact clone performance, despite available host resources.\n\n\n"}
